idpdiag-app-unknown-fix = Check the client ID the app is configured with, or register the app.
idpdiag-app-disabled = App { $client } is disabled: the authorization server answers invalid_client.
idpdiag-app-disabled-fix = Open the app and switch “Enabled” on.
idpdiag-app-redirect-ok = Redirect URI { $uri } is registered for { $client }.
idpdiag-app-redirect-unregistered = Redirect URI { $uri } is not registered for app { $client }. Registered: { $registered }. The sign-in page shows an error and never redirects.
idpdiag-app-redirect-unregistered-fix = Add the exact URI (scheme, host, port, path; no wildcard) to the app's redirect URIs, or fix the URI in the app.
idpdiag-endpoints-none = No FHIR endpoint is bound: tokens from this server are accepted nowhere.
idpdiag-endpoints-none-fix = Bind an endpoint under Settings → Endpoints.
idpdiag-endpoints-pending = The endpoints are bound after these checks pass; they are checked then.
idpdiag-endpoint-missing = Endpoint { $endpoint } is listed as bound but does not exist.
idpdiag-endpoint-missing-fix = Remove it from the bound endpoints, or recreate the endpoint.
idpdiag-endpoint-not-bound = Endpoint { $endpoint } is listed here but its Security settings trust { $actual }, not this server ({ $expected }): its tokens are refused there.
idpdiag-endpoint-not-bound-fix = Bind the endpoint again (Settings → Endpoints → Bind), or set its Security → Authorization server to Internal with this server.
idpdiag-endpoint-unlisted = Endpoint { $endpoint } trusts this server but is not in its bound endpoints: tokens are not issued for its audience.
idpdiag-endpoint-unlisted-fix = Add the endpoint to the bound endpoints.
idpdiag-endpoint-auth-off = Endpoint { $endpoint } trusts this server but its auth mode is Off: tokens are ignored and data is open.
idpdiag-endpoint-auth-off-fix = Set the endpoint's auth mode to Write-protect or Full.
idpdiag-endpoint-bound = Endpoint { $endpoint } accepts tokens from this server.
idpdiag-net-connect = Could not connect: { $detail }
idpdiag-net-connect-fix = The server could not reach its own public URL. Check HFS_BASE_URL / HFS_IDP_PUBLIC_BASE and the reverse proxy (nginx needs a location /idp/ rule), or set HFS_IDP_DIAGNOSTIC_VIA to the in-network address.
idpdiag-net-timeout = The request timed out: { $url }
idpdiag-net-timeout-fix = Check the reverse proxy and server load.
idpdiag-net-tls = TLS error: { $detail }
idpdiag-net-tls-fix = The TLS certificate of the public URL is not trusted by the server. Fix the certificate chain or set HFS_IDP_DIAGNOSTIC_VIA to the in-network address.
idpdiag-net-other = Request failed: { $detail }
idpdiag-net-other-fix = Check the public URL configuration.
idpdiag-doc-404 = No document at { $url } (404).
idpdiag-doc-404-fix = Check that HFS_IDP=on and the authorization server exists and is enabled; behind a proxy, route /idp/ and /.well-known/ to HFS.
idpdiag-doc-status = { $url } answered HTTP { $status }.
idpdiag-doc-status-fix = Look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-doc-not-json = { $url } answered with a web page, not JSON.
idpdiag-doc-not-json-fix = A proxy or another application answers this path. Route it to HFS.
idpdiag-clock-skew = The server's clock differs from this checker's by { $skew } s (limit { $limit } s): tokens may be refused as not yet valid or expired.
idpdiag-clock-skew-fix = Synchronise the clocks (NTP / chrony) of every HFS instance and of the reverse proxy.
idpdiag-clock-skew-token = The token's issue time is { $skew } s away from this checker's clock (limit { $limit } s): resource servers will refuse it as not yet valid or expired.
idpdiag-clock-skew-token-fix = Synchronise the clocks (NTP / chrony) of every HFS instance.
idpdiag-discovery-ok = The discovery document names the expected issuer.
idpdiag-issuer-mismatch = The discovery document says its issuer is { $actual }; expected exactly { $expected }. Every token would be refused.
idpdiag-issuer-mismatch-fix = Set HFS_IDP_PUBLIC_BASE (or HFS_BASE_URL) to the public origin users reach, without a trailing slash.
idpdiag-discovery-fields-ok = Required metadata fields are present.
idpdiag-discovery-fields-missing = Discovery lacks: { $fields }.
idpdiag-discovery-fields-missing-fix = This is a server defect; report it with the JSON report attached.
idpdiag-pkce-s256-only = PKCE S256 is advertised and plain is not.
idpdiag-pkce-advertised-wrong = PKCE methods advertised: { $methods }; expected S256 only.
idpdiag-pkce-advertised-wrong-fix = This is a server defect; report it.
idpdiag-endpoint-smart-ok = Endpoint { $endpoint } advertises this server and its capabilities.
idpdiag-endpoint-smart-other-issuer = Endpoint { $endpoint } advertises issuer { $actual }, not this server ({ $expected }). Apps launched against it sign in elsewhere.
idpdiag-endpoint-smart-other-issuer-fix = Bind the endpoint to this server (Settings → Endpoints → Bind) or set its Security → Authorization server to Internal.
idpdiag-endpoint-smart-capabilities = Endpoint { $endpoint } does not advertise { $missing } although this server has them on.
idpdiag-endpoint-smart-capabilities-fix = Bind the endpoint again so its SMART configuration is regenerated.
idpdiag-jwks-empty = The JWKS has no keys: no token can be verified.
idpdiag-jwks-empty-fix = Open Signing keys and generate keys (“Rotate now”).
idpdiag-jwks-public-only = { $count } published keys, no private members.
idpdiag-jwks-private-member = Keys { $kids } publish private key material!
idpdiag-jwks-private-member-fix = Emergency-rotate the keys immediately (Signing keys → Emergency rotation) and report the defect.
idpdiag-jwks-kid-thumbprint = Every kid is the key's RFC 7638 thumbprint.
idpdiag-jwks-kid-not-thumbprint = The kid differs from the RFC 7638 thumbprint for { $kids }.
idpdiag-jwks-kid-not-thumbprint-fix = Rotate the affected keys.
idpdiag-jwks-alg-ok = A { $alg } key is published.
idpdiag-jwks-alg-missing = { $alg } is advertised but no { $alg } key is published.
idpdiag-jwks-alg-missing-fix = Open Signing keys and rotate the missing algorithm.
idpdiag-jwks-cache-ok = Cache-Control: { $value }
idpdiag-jwks-cache-missing = The JWKS has no Cache-Control max-age; relying parties may refetch it on every request.
idpdiag-jwks-cache-missing-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-app-authorize-ok = App { $client } reaches the sign-in page with redirect URI { $uri }.
idpdiag-app-authorize-refused = App { $client } is refused at the authorization endpoint with redirect URI { $uri }.
idpdiag-app-authorize-refused-fix = See the Configuration step for the exact cause (disabled app, unregistered redirect URI).
idpdiag-code-flow-ok = Signed in through the hosted login form and exchanged the code with PKCE S256.
idpdiag-login-rejected = The sign-in page did not accept the test user { $user }: { $detail }
idpdiag-login-rejected-fix = Check the identity source (Local accounts) and the password policy; the test user is created with a policy-compliant password.
idpdiag-authorize-error-page = The authorization request stopped on an error page (HTTP { $status }): { $detail }
idpdiag-authorize-error-page-fix = The page text names the problem: typically an unknown or disabled app, an unregistered redirect URI, or an aud that is not a bound endpoint.
idpdiag-authorize-error = The authorization server answered error { $error }: { $detail }
idpdiag-authorize-error-fix = The description names the parameter. A common cause is an aud that is not a bound endpoint.
idpdiag-authorize-loop = The sign-in did not finish after 12 pages (redirect loop?).
idpdiag-authorize-loop-fix = Check the session cookie: behind a proxy the server must be reached over https for its __Host- cookie.
idpdiag-authorize-no-code = Redirected back without a code.
idpdiag-authorize-no-code-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-authorize-unexpected = Unexpected redirect.
idpdiag-authorize-unexpected-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-token-refused = The token endpoint refused the code: HTTP { $status } { $error } ({ $detail }).
idpdiag-token-refused-fix = The code or PKCE verifier was refused; look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-state-echoed = state was echoed.
idpdiag-state-not-echoed = state was not echoed correctly in the authorization response.
idpdiag-state-not-echoed-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-token-response-shape = The token response lacks access_token, token_type=Bearer or expires_in.
idpdiag-token-response-shape-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-access-token-ok = The access token verifies and carries iss, aud, scope, client_id and gid.
idpdiag-access-token-signature = The access token does not verify against the published keys: { $detail }
idpdiag-access-token-signature-fix = Usually a key signs before it is published. Open Signing keys; rotate again so the active key is published.
idpdiag-access-token-claims = Access token claims are wrong: { $detail }.
idpdiag-access-token-claims-fix = Check the endpoint binding (aud) and the public base URL (iss).
idpdiag-id-token-ok = The id_token verifies (signature, iss, aud, nonce, at_hash).
idpdiag-id-token-missing = scope openid was granted but no id_token was returned.
idpdiag-id-token-missing-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-id-token-signature = The id_token does not verify: { $detail }
idpdiag-id-token-signature-fix = Open Signing keys and check that an RS256 key is active and published.
idpdiag-id-token-claims = id_token claims are wrong: { $detail }.
idpdiag-id-token-claims-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-refresh-token-missing = offline_access was requested but no refresh token was issued.
idpdiag-refresh-token-missing-fix = Turn on “Refresh tokens (offline access)” in the capabilities.
idpdiag-redirect-refused = An unregistered redirect URI shows an error page and is never redirected to.
idpdiag-open-redirect = An unregistered redirect URI was redirected to: this is an open redirector.
idpdiag-open-redirect-fix = Server defect — do not use this authorization server until it is fixed; report it.
idpdiag-pkce-plain-refused = PKCE plain is refused.
idpdiag-pkce-plain-accepted = code_challenge_method=plain was accepted.
idpdiag-pkce-plain-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-verifier-refused = A wrong code_verifier gets invalid_grant.
idpdiag-verifier-accepted = A wrong code_verifier got HTTP { $status }.
idpdiag-verifier-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-code-replay-refused = A replayed code gets invalid_grant.
idpdiag-code-replay-revokes = The replay revoked the tokens of the first exchange.
idpdiag-code-replay-not-revoking = The replay did not revoke the tokens issued for the code.
idpdiag-code-replay-not-revoking-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-code-replay-accepted = A replayed code was accepted.
idpdiag-code-replay-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-fhir-read-ok = Endpoint { $endpoint } accepts the token for a read.
idpdiag-fhir-token-refused = Endpoint { $endpoint } refused the token (HTTP { $status }).
idpdiag-fhir-token-refused-fix = The endpoint does not trust this server, or expects another audience. Bind the endpoint (Settings → Endpoints) and check its Security page.
idpdiag-fhir-patient-missing = The token was accepted but the test patient does not exist on { $endpoint }.
idpdiag-fhir-patient-missing-fix = Use an existing Patient id for the test.
idpdiag-fhir-status = The FHIR read on { $endpoint } answered HTTP { $status }.
idpdiag-fhir-status-fix = Look at the endpoint's log for this request.
idpdiag-fhir-anonymous-refused = Without a token, { $endpoint } answers 401.
idpdiag-fhir-anonymous-open = Without a token, { $endpoint } answered data although its auth mode is Full.
idpdiag-fhir-anonymous-open-fix = Check the endpoint's auth mode and whether it inherits the server settings.
idpdiag-fhir-scope-enforced = A write with a read-only token is refused on { $endpoint }.
idpdiag-fhir-scope-not-enforced = A write with a read-only token got HTTP { $status } on { $endpoint } instead of 403.
idpdiag-fhir-scope-not-enforced-fix = Check the endpoint's auth mode (Write-protect/Full) and scope policy.
idpdiag-refresh-off = Refresh tokens are off for this authorization server.
idpdiag-refresh-rotated = Refreshing returned a new access token and a rotated refresh token.
idpdiag-refresh-not-rotated = The refresh token was not rotated.
idpdiag-refresh-not-rotated-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-refresh-refused = Refreshing failed: { $error } ({ $detail }).
idpdiag-refresh-refused-fix = Look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-refresh-reuse-refused = Reusing the old refresh token gets invalid_grant.
idpdiag-refresh-reuse-accepted = Reusing the old refresh token was accepted.
idpdiag-refresh-reuse-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-refresh-family-revoked = The reuse revoked the whole token family.
idpdiag-refresh-family-alive = After reuse, the newest refresh token still works.
idpdiag-refresh-family-alive-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-backend-off = Backend Services is off for this authorization server.
idpdiag-backend-ok = client_credentials with private_key_jwt issued a short-lived token.
idpdiag-backend-token-shape = Backend token: { $detail }.
idpdiag-backend-token-shape-fix = Check the backend token lifetime (≤ 300 s).
idpdiag-backend-refused = client_credentials was refused: { $error } ({ $detail }).
idpdiag-backend-refused-fix = Look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-assertion-replay-refused = A replayed client assertion (same jti) is refused.
idpdiag-assertion-replay-accepted = A replayed client assertion was accepted.
idpdiag-assertion-replay-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-assertion-exp-refused = An assertion valid for more than 5 minutes is refused.
idpdiag-assertion-exp-accepted = An assertion valid for one hour was accepted.
idpdiag-assertion-exp-accepted-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-introspection-off = Introspection is off for this authorization server.
idpdiag-introspection-active = A live token introspects as active with its scope and context.
idpdiag-introspection-fields = Active, but missing { $fields }.
idpdiag-introspection-fields-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-introspection-inactive = A live token introspects as inactive.
idpdiag-introspection-inactive-fix = Server defect, or the grant was revoked by an earlier step; report it.
idpdiag-introspection-refused = Introspection answered { $error } ({ $detail }).
idpdiag-introspection-refused-fix = Look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-introspection-garbage-inactive = A garbage token introspects as inactive.
idpdiag-introspection-garbage-active = A garbage token introspects as active!
idpdiag-introspection-garbage-active-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-introspection-garbage-error = Introspecting a garbage token did not answer active:false.
idpdiag-introspection-garbage-error-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-revocation-off = Revocation is off for this authorization server.
idpdiag-revoke-ok = Revocation answered 200.
idpdiag-revoke-status = Revocation did not answer 200.
idpdiag-revoke-status-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-revoked-inactive = The revoked token introspects as inactive.
idpdiag-revoked-still-active = The revoked token still introspects as active.
idpdiag-revoked-still-active-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-revoked-fhir-refused = Endpoint { $endpoint } refuses the revoked token.
idpdiag-revoked-fhir-accepted = Endpoint { $endpoint } still accepted the revoked token after { $secs } s.
idpdiag-revoked-fhir-accepted-fix = With the compatibility binding (External issuer = this server), revocation reaches the endpoint only at token expiry. Switch the endpoint's provider to Internal for immediate revocation.
idpdiag-oidc-off = OpenID Connect is off.
idpdiag-userinfo-ok = userinfo sub equals the id_token sub.
idpdiag-userinfo-sub-mismatch = userinfo sub differs from the id_token sub.
idpdiag-userinfo-sub-mismatch-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-userinfo-status = userinfo did not answer 200.
idpdiag-userinfo-status-fix = Look at the server log for this request.
idpdiag-logout-not-advertised = No end_session_endpoint is advertised.
idpdiag-logout-not-advertised-fix = Turn on OpenID Connect.
idpdiag-logout-ok = After sign-out, a silent sign-in (prompt=none) answers login_required.
idpdiag-logout-session-alive = After sign-out the session still signs in silently.
idpdiag-logout-session-alive-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-logout-prompt-none-unexpected = After sign-out, prompt=none answered unexpectedly: { $detail }
idpdiag-logout-prompt-none-unexpected-fix = Server defect; report it.
idpdiag-token-already-expired = The token is already expired when received.
idpdiag-token-already-expired-fix = Check token lifetimes and the server clock.
idpdiag-skipped-dependency = Skipped: it depends on step “{ $step }”, which failed.
idpdiag-fixture-failed = Could not create the temporary test app or user: { $detail }
idpdiag-fixture-failed-fix = Enable at least one launch mode and client type in the capabilities so a test app can be registered.
